+# Opt-in trim for weak tool-callers (small local models, and any route whose
+# request-size limits a large toolset blows past -- see
+# security-scan/strix-local-poc/windows-wsl-ollama-setup.md for why this
+# exists). Drops bookkeeping tools (notes/coverage/threat-model), MCP
+# dispatch tools (irrelevant with zero MCP connections configured, and the
+# exact tool whose schema blocked every Groq request before the separate
+# groq-empty-schema.patch), and multi-agent orchestration tools (unused by
+# a single root agent that never spawns children). Enable with
+# STRIX_MINIMAL_TOOLS=1. Todo tools are kept on purpose: a weak model
+# benefits from being able to write down "step 1 / step 2 / step 3" and
+# check them off, which is exactly what was missing when it drifted into
+# pointless ls/pwd loops (see the same notes file). Vulnerability/dependency
+# reporting, requests, sitemap, scope rules, web search and shell/
+# filesystem tools are kept -- those are what an actual scan needs to
+# produce a result.
